-- The result. Every premise is the field's own; the inference is his. Synesthesia is defined by an
-- inducer that automatically, involuntarily evokes an experience not physically present. Stroop
-- (1935): a literate person cannot not read a word; the field certifies synesthetes with exactly
-- this interference (the synesthetic Stroop). Dehaene et al. (Science 330:1359, 2010; illiterate,
-- adult-literate and child-literate adults): literacy enhances phonological activation to speech in
-- the planum temporale and gives top-down activation of orthography from spoken input, even when
-- literacy comes in adulthood: a two-way coupling of sight and sound that evolution never supplied.
-- Silent reading activates sound (homophone errors, ROWS read as ROSE; auditory cortex responding to
-- text). So literacy is a synesthesia between visual patterns and sounds, built by a procedure
-- (schooling) in most of humanity: trainability of synesthesia is a theorem with billions of
-- witnesses, and language is a cognitive technology for constructing senses evolution did not give.
-- The field's miss, with its own evidence in hand: Bor, Rothen, Schwartzman, Clayton, Seth (Sci Rep
